   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general municipal law, in relation to insurance reserve\nfunds of certain school districts",
    "basePrintNo": "S1737",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1737-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §6-n, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1737\n\nSPONSOR: JACOBS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law, in relation to insurance\nreserve funds of certain school districts\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill will allow certain school districts who have elected to self-\ninsure to establish an insurance reserve fund.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 Amends paragraph (a) of subdivision 2 of section 6-n of the\ngeneral municipal law by providing certain school districts the ability\nto establish an insurance reserve fund.\n\nSection 2 is the enacting clause\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn order to prudently manage the rising costs of health insurance,\ncertain school districts have elected to self-insure its health benefit\nprogram. Self-insurance offers many advantages for school district and\nits employees, however under current law, school districts are prevented\nfrom retaining more than four percent of their budget in an unappropri-\nated fund balance. Authorizing certain school districts to establish an\ninsurance reserve fund will allow them to manage year-to-year variabil-\nity in claims.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS.7786 (2017-2018) Died in Local Government\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
